=\\frac{20}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(20-1)(-2)) \\\\ -160 & =10(2{a}_{1}-38) \\\\ -16 & =2{a}_{1}-38 \\\\ 22 & =2{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{1} & =11.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-5606/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9f9251ee-4d19-5074-a2a3-07e13149260f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-5606"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-250844/field-1/15ee7994f213b4b15d718ff51a8597a12c4d7ebb8192568a04d381a17409172d" :answer/id #uuid "93326fab-65bb-5b4e-9d6b-5b7ca3c19f7d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-0.8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186075762 :answer-field/choices ["q-250844/field-1/15ee7994f213b4b15d718ff51a8597a12c4d7ebb8192568a04d381a17409172d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-250844"] :question/problem "If the sum of the first $20$ terms of an arithmetic series is ${S}_{20}=301,$ and the common difference is $d=1.5,$ then the first term of the series is ${a}_{1}=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "We are given the common difference of the series. So, to find the first term, we use the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series in the form\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d),\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1}$ is the first term, $d$ is the common difference, and $N$ is the number of terms.\n\nSubstituting $N=20$, $d=1.5$, and ${S}_{N}=301$ into the formula above, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}301 & =\\frac{20}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(20-1)(1.5)) \\\\ 301 & =10(2{a}_{1}+28.5) \\\\ 30.1 & =2{a}_{1}+28.5 \\\\ 1.6 & =2{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{1} & =0.8.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-233995/field-1/f18416f35432d431c72acfc39d7e01add033f359c3a10a94fc360561f773edf6" :answer/id #uuid "7f9dcafe-d6f6-5fff-897d-d70c4ed4d07f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "53" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-233995/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "f98866ee-ac4e-5beb-a49b-75832a45d69b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-233995/field-1/f18416f35432d431c72acfc39d7e01add033f359c3a10a94fc360561f773edf6" :answer-field/choices ["q-233995/field-1/f18416f35432d431c72acfc39d7e01add033f359c3a10a94fc360561f773edf6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-233995" :question/id #uuid "05161e8f-e95d-5bde-9b69-96629df57e04" :question/math-academy-id "q-233995" :question/problem "If the sum of the first $29$ terms of an arithmetic series is ${S}_{29}=319,$ and the common difference is $d=-3,$ then the first term of the series is ${a}_{1}=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "We are given the common difference of the series. So, to find the first term, we use the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series in the form\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d),\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1}$ is the first term, $d$ is the common difference, and $N$ is the number of terms.\n\nSubstituting $N=29$, $d=-3$, and ${S}_{N}=319$ into the formula above, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}319 & =\\frac{29}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(29-1)(-3)) \\\\ 638 & =29(2{a}_{1}-84) \\\\ 22 & =2{a}_{1}-84 \\\\ 106 & =2{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{1} & =53.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-233995/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9f9251ee-4d19-5074-a2a3-07e13149260f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-233995"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-5602"] :question/problem "What is the first term of an arithmetic series if the common difference is $d=-4,$ and the sum of the first $20$ terms is ${S}_{20}=1\\,160?$" :question/worked-solution "We are given the common difference of the series. So, to find the first term, we use the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series in the form\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d),\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1}$ is the first term, $d$ is the common difference, and $N$ is the number of terms.\n\nSubstituting $N=20$, $d=-4$, and ${S}_{N}=1\\,160$ into the formula above, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1\\,160 & =\\frac{20}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(20-1)(-4)) \\\\ 1\\,160 & =10(2{a}_{1}-76) \\\\ 116 & =2{a}_{1}-76 \\\\ 192 & =2{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{1} & =96.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-250834/field-1/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" :answer/id #uuid "1b96b99e-5c2c-5c3c-917c-eff2002dd3e4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-250834/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "e24fdcde-54c5-50a2-a9cd-743d36dd1602" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-250834/field-1/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" :answer-field/choices ["q-250834/field-1/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-250834" :question/id #uuid "40ae85a2-da7c-5fcc-8fba-db8deb8365ac" :question/math-academy-id "q-250834" :question/problem "If the sum of the first $36$ terms of an arithmetic series is ${S}_{36}=2\\,142,$ and the common difference is $d=3,$ then the first term of the series is ${a}_{1}=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "We are given the common difference of the series. So, to find the first term, we use the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series in the form\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d),\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1}$ is the first term, $d$ is the common difference, and $N$ is the number of terms.\n\nSubstituting $N=36$, $d=3$, and ${S}_{N}=2\\,142$ into the formula above, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\,142 & =\\frac{36}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(36-1)(3)) \\\\ 2\\,142 & =18(2{a}_{1}+105) \\\\ 119 & =2{a}_{1}+105 \\\\ 14 & =2{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{1} & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-250834/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9f9251ee-4d19-5074-a2a3-07e13149260f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-250834"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-233997/field-1/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" :answer/id #uuid "2b1ac7ad-3077-5894-809d-9a4624a97ca4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186075694 :answer-field/choices ["q-233997/field-1/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-233997"] :question/problem "If the $15$th term of an arithmetic series is $-53$ and the sum of the first $21$ terms is $-777,$ then the first term of the series is ${a}_{1}=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "We are given one term of the series. So, to find the first term, we use the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series in the form\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d),\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1}$ is the first term, $d$ is the common difference, and $N$ is the number of terms.\n\nSubstituting $N=21$ and ${S}_{N}=-777$ into the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d) \\\\ -777 & =\\frac{21}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(21-1)d) \\\\ -1\\,554= & 21(2{a}_{1}+20d) \\\\ -74 & =2{a}_{1}+20d.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, we can write an equation for the $15$th term of the arithmetic series and substitute in its known value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}+(n-1)d \\\\ {a}_{15} & ={a}_{1}+(15-1)d \\\\ -53 & ={a}_{1}+14d\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, we obtain the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-53={a}_{1}+14d \\\\ -74=2{a}_{1}+20d\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve this system, we multiply the first equation by $-2$ and add the result to the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}106 & =-2{a}_{1}-28d \\\\ -74 & =2{a}_{1}+20d \\\\ 32 & =-8d \\\\ d & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $d=-4$ into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-53 & ={a}_{1}+14d \\\\ -53 & ={a}_{1}+14(-4) \\\\ -53 & ={a}_{1}-56 \\\\ {a}_{1} & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-250881/field-1/3224ab5f6f5fb64621a714f7654c4df06661a69e7edb8f5993dcef1e46ce3dea" :answer/id #uuid "42476e40-c10c-542c-a508-59f13940c25e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-250881/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "3df3aa0a-3535-5e13-9c81-f69f91a522a0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-250881/field-1/3224ab5f6f5fb64621a714f7654c4df06661a69e7edb8f5993dcef1e46ce3dea" :answer-field/choices ["q-250881/field-1/3224ab5f6f5fb64621a714f7654c4df06661a69e7edb8f5993dcef1e46ce3dea"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-250881" :question/id #uuid "f12cd0e2-1bab-50a8-952e-2186b606facf" :question/math-academy-id "q-250881" :question/problem "If the $6$th term of an arithmetic series is $\\frac{37}{4}$ and the sum of the first $16$ terms is $228,$ then the first term of the series is ${a}_{1}=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "We are given one term of the series. So, to find the first term, we use the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series in the form\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d),\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1}$ is the first term, $d$ is the common difference, and $N$ is the number of terms.\n\nSubstituting $N=16$ and ${S}_{N}=228$ into the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d) \\\\ 228 & =\\frac{16}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(16-1)d) \\\\ 228 & =8(2{a}_{1}+15d) \\\\ \\frac{57}{2} & =2{a}_{1}+15d.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, we can write an equation for the $6$th term of the arithmetic series and substitute in its known value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}+(n-1)d \\\\ {a}_{6} & ={a}_{1}+(6-1)d \\\\ \\frac{37}{4} & ={a}_{1}+5d\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, we obtain the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{37}{4}={a}_{1}+5d \\\\ \\frac{57}{2}=2{a}_{1}+15d\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve this system, we multiply the first equation by $-2$ and add the result to the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{37}{2} & =-2{a}_{1}-10d \\\\ \\frac{57}{2} & =2{a}_{1}+15d \\\\ \\frac{20}{2} & =5d \\\\ d & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $d=2$ into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{37}{4} & ={a}_{1}+5d \\\\ \\frac{37}{4} & ={a}_{1}+5(2) \\\\ \\frac{37}{4} & ={a}_{1}+\\frac{40}{4} \\\\ {a}_{1} & =-\\frac{3}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-250881/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "07a3dfec-3f7b-5820-9be5-12bf4acd5a3b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-250881"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-250863/field-1/286fb92e9ba180b012d241bb7e762701483c9c864420d9df6597147f2e2fb458" :answer/id #uuid "fc5503ee-1b46-5288-b69d-63e1a8800d95" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "28" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-250863/field-1/94b1e608a1bece13c117321c62644f2051416b0003719c2dd4b9ea44af9d6b64" :answer/id #uuid "f0d7afa3-bd90-5a65-8996-bc2a5a545bda" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-28" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-250863/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "17cd7f1e-32a6-52ac-a9c7-4007ea2c9e45" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-250863/field-1/286fb92e9ba180b012d241bb7e762701483c9c864420d9df6597147f2e2fb458" :answer-field/choices ["q-250863/field-1/286fb92e9ba180b012d241bb7e762701483c9c864420d9df6597147f2e2fb458" "q-250863/field-1/94b1e608a1bece13c117321c62644f2051416b0003719c2dd4b9ea44af9d6b64"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-250863" :question/id #uuid "a22c14f9-3812-5d88-ba4b-6e25ffa53a6c" :question/math-academy-id "q-250863" :question/problem "If the $16$th term of an arithmetic series is $-32$ and the sum of the first $20$ terms is $-200,$ then the first term of the series is ${a}_{1}=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "We are given one term of the series. So, to find the first term, we use the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series in the form\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d),\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1}$ is the first term, $d$ is the common difference, and $N$ is the number of terms.\n\nSubstituting $N=20$ and ${S}_{N}=-200$ into the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d) \\\\ -200 & =\\frac{20}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(20-1)d) \\\\ -200 & =10(2{a}_{1}+19d) \\\\ -20 & =2{a}_{1}+19d.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, we can write an equation for the $16$th term of the arithmetic series and substitute in its known value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}+(n-1)d \\\\ {a}_{16} & ={a}_{1}+(16-1)d \\\\ -32 & ={a}_{1}+15d\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, we obtain the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-32={a}_{1}+15d \\\\ -20=2{a}_{1}+19d\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve this system, we multiply the first equation by $-2$ and add the result to the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}64 & =-2{a}_{1}-30d \\\\ -20 & =2{a}_{1}+19d \\\\ 44 & =-11d \\\\ d & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $d=-4$ into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-32 & ={a}_{1}+15d \\\\ -32 & ={a}_{1}+15(-4) \\\\ -32 & ={a}_{1}-60 \\\\ {a}_{1} & =28.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-250863/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "07a3dfec-3f7b-5820-9be5-12bf4acd5a3b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-250863"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-250878/field-1/3a619fab2616dab0463f9c76cb72cd9f101e45e62111356a5b0b111e062a8dcf" :answer/id #uuid "ae3d69e5-d4d7-5a0c-887b-877ab32d5b4f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-250878/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "ae44cffe-4ac1-54af-8af0-6bb954e5528b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-250878/field-1/3a619fab2616dab0463f9c76cb72cd9f101e45e62111356a5b0b111e062a8dcf" :answer-field/choices ["q-250878/field-1/3a619fab2616dab0463f9c76cb72cd9f101e45e62111356a5b0b111e062a8dcf"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-250878" :question/id #uuid "071ccade-a6f8-5e6b-af5a-bbbc446621b5" :question/math-academy-id "q-250878" :question/problem "If the $9$th term of an arithmetic series is $\\frac{46}{3}$ and the sum of the first $15$ terms is $200,$ then the first term of the series is ${a}_{1}=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "We are given one term of the series. So, to find the first term, we use the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series in the form\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d),\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1}$ is the first term, $d$ is the common difference, and $N$ is the number of terms.\n\nSubstituting $N=15$ and ${S}_{N}=200$ into the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d) \\\\ 200 & =\\frac{15}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(15-1)d) \\\\ 400 & =15(2{a}_{1}+14d) \\\\ \\frac{400}{15} & =2{a}_{1}+14d \\\\ \\frac{80}{3} & =2{a}_{1}+14d.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, we can write an equation for the $9$th term of the arithmetic series and substitute in its known value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}+(n-1)d \\\\ {a}_{9} & ={a}_{1}+(9-1)d \\\\ \\frac{46}{3} & ={a}_{1}+8d\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, we obtain the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{46}{3}={a}_{1}+8d \\\\ \\frac{80}{3}=2{a}_{1}+14d\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve this system, we multiply the first equation by $-2$ and add the result to the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{92}{3} & =-2{a}_{1}-16d \\\\ \\frac{80}{3} & =2{a}_{1}+14d \\\\ -\\frac{12}{3} & =-2d \\\\ d & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $d=2$ into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{46}{3} & ={a}_{1}+8d \\\\ \\frac{46}{3} & ={a}_{1}+8(2) \\\\ \\frac{46}{3} & ={a}_{1}+16 \\\\ \\frac{46}{3} & ={a}_{1}+\\frac{48}{3} \\\\ {a}_{1} & =-\\frac{2}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-250878/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "07a3dfec-3f7b-5820-9be5-12bf4acd5a3b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-250878"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-108724/selection/4ba07d595da94e6c18190f4c7e9ba4b4ed6a582ffd72c14b8d2af03cbda7a38b" :answer/id #uuid "4c0fb856-acd1-5082-b7f3-6d9e0d0bc587" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.92" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108724/selection/36f411d803d3d277481a0781d98c8e9c64d97ae3b1730405e61a65241c2d48e5" :answer/id #uuid "5bac4b7d-1f57-5b55-82d6-af462dc60784" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.64" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108724/selection/15d0f56b668f72c799a6e0ecc1e4659b388db75a82effccc4d668d11c9cd442d" :answer/id #uuid "7ae6a22c-8d11-56c2-9596-d174a31c2231" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.45" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108724/selection/dbf2e7fe931e9c14f7f394ddcdf822e332bb4de32324f3750f476fbcc7256c26" :answer/id #uuid "2b61e236-ca99-58e9-bd83-db330903c91e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1.36" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108724/selection/c9593fef8797b3108e7c11a13ebdd5c82dd440e8f5de7a2b295f42f3aa123295" :answer/id #uuid "cbb6df4f-c778-5ae1-b175-ce811f2b470c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.56" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108724/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "1eb10240-d1f1-5001-949d-bced3721068b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-108724/selection/36f411d803d3d277481a0781d98c8e9c64d97ae3b1730405e61a65241c2d48e5" :answer-field/choices ["q-108724/selection/4ba07d595da94e6c18190f4c7e9ba4b4ed6a582ffd72c14b8d2af03cbda7a38b" "q-108724/selection/36f411d803d3d277481a0781d98c8e9c64d97ae3b1730405e61a65241c2d48e5" "q-108724/selection/15d0f56b668f72c799a6e0ecc1e4659b388db75a82effccc4d668d11c9cd442d" "q-108724/selection/dbf2e7fe931e9c14f7f394ddcdf822e332bb4de32324f3750f476fbcc7256c26" "q-108724/selection/c9593fef8797b3108e7c11a13ebdd5c82dd440e8f5de7a2b295f42f3aa123295"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-108724" :question/id #uuid "60e9a618-f20a-5ccf-9c10-25260f7c4404" :question/math-academy-id "q-108724" :question/problem "Find the first term of an arithmetic series if its $5$th term is $-0.28$ and the sum of the first $12$ terms of the series is $-12.$" :question/worked-solution "We are given one term of the series. So, to find the first term, we use the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series in the form\n\n$$\n{S}_{N}=\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d),\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{1}$ is the first term, $d$ is the common difference, and $N$ is the number of terms.\n\nSubstituting $N=12$ and ${S}_{N}=-12$ into the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d) \\\\ -12 & =\\frac{12}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(12-1)d) \\\\ -12 & =6(2{a}_{1}+11d) \\\\ -2 & =2{a}_{1}+11d.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, we can write an equation for the $5$th term of the arithmetic series and substitute in its known value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}+(n-1)d \\\\ {a}_{5} & ={a}_{1}+(5-1)d \\\\ -0.28 & ={a}_{1}+4d\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, we obtain the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-0.28={a}_{1}+4d \\\\ -2=2{a}_{1}+11d\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve this system, we multiply the first equation by $-2$ and add the result to the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0.56 & =-2{a}_{1}-8d \\\\ -2 & =2{a}_{1}+11d \\\\ -1.44 & =3d \\\\ d & =-0.48\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $d=-0.48$ into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-0.28 & ={a}_{1}+4(-0.48) \\\\ -0.28 & ={a}_{1}-1.92 \\\\ {a}_{1} & =1.64.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-108724/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "07a3dfec-3f7b-5820-9be5-12bf4acd5a3b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-108724"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-4206"] :question/problem "If the sum of the first $20$ terms of an arithmetic series is $S_{20}=560,$ and the last term is $a_{20}=66,$ what is the first term of the series?" :question/worked-solution "We are given the last term of our series. So, to find the first term, we use the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series in the form\n\n$$\nS_N = \\dfrac{N}{2}(a_1+a_N),\n$$\n\nwhere $a_1$ is the first term, $a_N$ is the last term, and $N$ is the number of terms.\n\nSubstituting $a_{20}=66,$ $N=20,$ and $S_N=560$ into the formula above and solving for $a_1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}560 & =\\frac{20}{2}({a}_{1}+66) \\\\ 560 & =10({a}_{1}+66) \\\\ \\frac{560}{10} & ={a}_{1}+66 \\\\ 56 & ={a}_{1}+66 \\\\ {a}_{1} & =-10.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-4207"] :question/problem "What is the first term of an arithmetic series if the common difference is $d=2,$ and the sum of the first $50$ terms is $S_{50}=2\\,150?$" :question/worked-solution "We are given the common difference of the series. So, to find the first term, we use the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series in the form\n\n$$\nS_N = \\dfrac{N}{2}\\big( 2a_1+(N-1)d \\big),\n$$\n\nwhere $a_1$ is the first term, $d$ is the common difference, and $N$ is the number of terms.\n\nSubstituting $N=50,$ $d=2,$ and $S_N=2\\,150$ into the formula above and solving for $a_1,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\,150 & =\\frac{50}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(50-1)(2)) \\\\ 4\\,300 & =50(2{a}_{1}+98) \\\\ \\frac{4\\,300}{50} & =2{a}_{1}+98 \\\\ 86 & =2{a}_{1}+98 \\\\ -12 & =2{a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{1} & =-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-4208"] :question/problem "Find the first term of an arithmetic series if its $11$th term is $29$ and the sum of the first $16$ terms of the series is $384.$" :question/worked-solution "We are given one term of the series. So, to find the first term, we use the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series in the form\n\n$$\nS_N = \\dfrac{N}{2}\\left( 2a_1+(N-1)d \\right),\n$$\n\nwhere $a_1$ is the first term, $d$ is the common difference, and $N$ is the number of terms.\n\nSubstituting $N = 16$ and $S_N = 384$ into the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{S}_{N} & =\\frac{N}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(N-1)d) \\\\ 384 & =\\frac{16}{2}(2{a}_{1}+(16-1)d) \\\\ 384 & =8(2{a}_{1}+15d) \\\\ \\frac{384}{8} & =2{a}_{1}+15d \\\\ 48 & =2{a}_{1}+15d.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, we can write an equation for the $11$th term of the arithmetic series and substitute in its known value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}+(n-1)d \\\\ {a}_{11} & ={a}_{1}+(11-1)d \\\\ 29 & ={a}_{1}+10d\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, we obtain the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}29={a}_{1}+10d \\\\ 48=2{a}_{1}+15d\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve this system, we multiply the first equation by $-2$ and add the result to the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-58 & =-2{a}_{1}-20d \\\\ 48 & =2{a}_{1}+15d \\\\ -10 & =-5d \\\\ d & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $d = 2$ into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}29 & ={a}_{1}+10(2) \\\\ 29 & ={a}_{1}+20 \\\\ {a}_{1} & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
